<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 242 nm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Code-to-model traceability: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 functions are named for the sweep, the ablation, the segmentation and the goodness-of-fit, and the docstring still cites Turing 1952 and Schnakenberg 1979. The Lean module still has five sorry-free theorems for the 242 nm window, the ratio 31.18 above onset 13.605, the 1452 nm domain, the equal-diffusion sign, and the zero Holocene offset. Deducted because those theorems are integer witnesses rather than a real-analysis derivation of sigma(k)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 242 nm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The Pass 1 Schnakenberg linearisation and the fastest-mode solve are unchanged and still give sigma(k_c)=0.2415 at 242 nm. Pass 2 adds the simulated equal-diffusion trajectory, which collapses, matching the sign of the analytic control. Deducted because the saturated FFT peak is 284.76 nm: nonlinear spot spacing is coarser than the linear carrier, and the script does not add a wavenumber-selection term that pulls the spots back onto 242 nm." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0.py L243–L260: Nonlinear FFT peak 284.76 nm versus the linear 242 nm carrier <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0c76d15d/models/2026-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L243-L260>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 242 nm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
