<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 242 nm (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii)",
        "Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 242 nm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Pixel-level prediction of the gallery spiral, a species-level identification of the Wikimedia valve, or equality of the 284.76 nm nonlinear spacing with the 242 nm linear carrier.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The GIF last frame uses gallery-envelope weight 0.55. The unguided three-ocellus field is retained and its spatial correlation (0.071) is reported separately.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: a=0.062, b=1.35, D_v/D_u=31.18 lock the linear carrier at 242 nm. Pass 2 sweeps the ratio, simulates the equal-diffusion collapse, segments both images, and reports Pearson, RMSE and KS.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 supplies the mass-action kinetics used here.",
        "reported_in_source: Sumper 2002 and Lenoci & Camp 2008 relate diatom nanopatterns to polyamine phase separation in the silica deposition vesicle.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite wavenumber when inhibitor diffusion sufficiently exceeds activator diffusion.",
        "reported_in_source: Yendo & Akatsuka 1910 observed living A. ehrenbergii, fixing this chronoseries at Holocene, 0 Ma.",
        "transfer_boundary: 242 nm is the assigned detail scale, not a published A. ehrenbergii pore measurement. The gallery frame is a 100 μm stylized image. The Wikimedia file is Arachnoidiscus sp.",
        "transfer_boundary: Radial Pearson 0.986 is between the gallery and the envelope-mixed frame, not between the gallery and the unguided activator." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "IV. Protista & Monera" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mineralized Protists (Silica/Calcite)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Arachnoidiscus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/arachnoidiscus_ehrenbergii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite wavenumber when inhibitor diffusion sufficiently exceeds activator diffusion. | Schnakenberg 1979 supplies the mass-action kinetics used here. | Sumper 2002 and Lenoci & Camp 2008 relate diatom nanopatterns to polyamine phase separation in the silica deposition vesicle. | Yendo & Akatsuka 1910 observed living A. ehrenbergii, fixing this chronoseries at Holocene, 0 Ma.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.062, b=1.35, D_v/D_u=31.18 lock the linear carrier at 242 nm. Pass 2 sweeps the ratio, simulates the equal-diffusion collapse, segments both images, and reports Pearson, RMSE and KS. | The GIF last frame uses gallery-envelope weight 0.55. The unguided three-ocellus field is retained and its spatial correlation (0.071) is reported separately.; transfer_boundary: 242 nm is the assigned detail scale, not a published A. ehrenbergii pore measurement. The gallery frame is a 100 μm stylized image. The Wikimedia file is Arachnoidiscus sp. | Radial Pearson 0.986 is between the gallery and the envelope-mixed frame, not between the gallery and the unguided activator.; does_not_claim: Pixel-level prediction of the gallery spiral, a species-level identification of the Wikimedia valve, or equality of the 284.76 nm nonlinear spacing with the 242 nm linear carrier.]; phenomenon_size: 144 nm (1.44e-07 m, log10=-6.842 m, tier=2_macromolecular_100nm); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 144 nm to 450 µm): 144 nm:arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-bioelectric-polarity, 538 nm:arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-vertex-packing, 10 µm:arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength, 19 µm:arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-clock-wavefront, 43 µm:arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-elastic-buckling, 58 µm:arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-morphogen-condensation, 76 µm:arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-flux-canalization, 100 µm:arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-branching-tree" ;
